---
description: Seeder probes must never leave hung aria2c or TEMP junk
alwaysApply: true
---

# Probe cleanup (mandatory)

When running `mrf find` / `mrf test-hash` / hash checks:

- Prefer `uv run mrf test-hash` / find's built-in probe (hard-kills aria2c, deletes temp `mrf-test`).
- After any hash probe: confirm no leftover `aria2c` with `mrf-test` in the command line; kill if present.
- Delete scam/junk `.torrent` caches the user rejected (under `torrents/`).
- find / download must inspect before probe/download; never download `Verdict=scam`.
- Never treat a seeder probe as a real download — real downloads only via `uv run mrf download` into `downloads/`.
- If the user reports "something is downloading" after a find/test, check/kill probe `aria2c` first.
